SECTION 1 (TCA 39-17-1301, new definition): "Assault weapon" means: (A) (i) A selective-fire firearm capable of fully automatic, semiautomatic, or burst fire at the option of the user or any of the following specified semiautomatic firearms:
SECTION 1 (TCA 39-17-1301, new definition, (E)): (E) Any semiautomatic firearm regardless of whether such firearm is listed in subdivisions ( )(A) - (D) if the firearm is: (ii) A semiautomatic, centerfire rifle that has a fixed magazine with the ability to accept more than ten (10) rounds; (iii) A semiautomatic, centerfire rifle that has an overall length of less than thirty inches (30"); (vii) A semiautomatic shotgun that has the ability to accept a detachable magazine; or (viii) A shotgun with a revolving cylinder;
SECTION 2 (TCA 39-17-1302(a)): (4) An assault weapon;
SECTION 3 (TCA 39-17-1302(c)): ( ) If the weapon is an assault weapon as described in subdivision (a)(4), then the person possessed the weapon prior to July 1, 2024;
SECTION 4 (TCA 39-17-1302, new subsection): (1) A person in possession of an assault weapon prior to July 1, 2024, must apply for a certificate of possession by July 1, 2025. (4) A person who obtains ownership by bequest or intestate succession of an assault weapon for which a certificate of possession has been issued under this section shall, within ninety (90) days: (A) Render the assault weapon permanently inoperable; (B) Sell the assault weapon to a licensed gun dealer; or (C) Remove the assault weapon from this state.
SECTION 5 (TCA 39-17-1302(d)): Tennessee Code Annotated, Section 39-17-1302(d), is amended by deleting the language "subdivisions (a)(3) or (a)(4)" and substituting instead the language "subdivision (a)(3)".
